; Belisarius — standalone adaptive Byzantine AI player.
; New project. Sources: stock AI + Naga patterns only.
; No dependency on any Byzantine.* experiment.
; Prompt 1 of 10: foundation + decision-loop skeleton.
; Prompt 2 of 10: observation + decaying memory + purposeful scouting.
; Prompt 3 of 10: interpretation + opponent model + prediction.
; Prompt 4 of 10: strategy selection + opening execution/deviation.
; Prompt 5 of 10: economy engine (allocation, timing, villagers, farms, builders, market).
; Prompt 6 of 10: production + composition + counter-counter + upgrades + power spikes.
; Prompt 7 of 10: positioning + engagement + retreat + micro + target priority.
; Prompt 8 of 10: raids + multi-prong + defense + buildings + map + siege/monks/relics.
; Prompt 9 of 10: adaptation (verify, abandon, winning/losing, late game, identity).
; Prompt 10 of 10: final integration (water, team, triage, endgame, one player).
; Arbitration rebuild P1: resource commitment ledger + spend gates.
; Arbitration rebuild P2: Dark food lifecycle + farm demand.
; Arbitration rebuild P3: age-transition prep + Imperial tech + timing.
; Arbitration rebuild P4: demand-driven military (deficit, buildings, mass, hook).
; Content rebuild C1: food transition + forecast.
; Content rebuild C2: skeletons + boom TC demand + Castle villager flood.
; Content rebuild C4: mobility branch + memory decay + stop rules.
; Content rebuild C5: objective clock + role relevance.
; Loop: OBSERVE -> INTERPRET -> PREDICT -> PRIORITIZE -> PLAN -> ACT -> VERIFY -> ADAPT -> OBSERVE.
